[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mReassess K3s And Kubernetes Workloads\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Reassess bearing VDcStSMlp against the now-verified installable developer experience, hybrid execution, and storage foundations, and convert that bearing into the next explicit board state for K3s work. (\u001b[2mVDcStSMlp\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this K3s reassessment visible through mission, bearing-list, and flow surfaces. (\u001b[2mrun `just keel mission show VDfqti68W`, `just keel mission next VDfqti68W`, `just keel bearing list`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor`\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVDcStSMlp\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - K3s And Kubernetes Workloads (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n  Bearings (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[94mVDcStSMlp\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - K3s And Kubernetes Workloads (\u001b[2mlaid\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-12T10:13:14\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VDfqti68W/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Reassess K3s And Kubernetes Workloads - Charter\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Reassess bearing VDcStSMlp against the now-verified installable developer experience, hybrid execution, and storage foundations, and convert that bearing into the next explicit board state for K3s work. | board: VDcStSMlp |\r\n| MG-02 | Keep the mission surfaces doctor-clean and make this K3s reassessment visible through mission, bearing-list, and flow surfaces. | manual: run `just keel mission show VDfqti68W`, `just keel mission next VDfqti68W`, `just keel bearing list`, `just flow`, and `just keel doctor` |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Keep the first K3s outcome narrow: one canonical operator workflow and one bounded cluster or service slice, not a generic Kubernetes platform promise.\r\n- Use bearing VDcStSMlp plus the now-verified installable, hybrid, and storage artifacts as the primary sources, and do not broaden scope into GPU work unless the reassessment exposes a concrete dependency.\r\n- Preserve the hard-cutover policy: do not add compatibility bridges or parallel orchestration contracts just to keep multiple Kubernetes shapes alive.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while any MG-* goal has unfinished board work\r\n- HALT when VDcStSMlp has been converted into an explicit next board state and only manual verification remains\r\n- YIELD to human when prioritization depends on provider choice, control-plane topology, or external cluster commitments that are not inferable from the repository\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VDcStSMlp\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mK3s And Kubernetes Workloads\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 10:36:47\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 10:47:38\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-12 14:50:26\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-12 14:50:26\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m4h 2m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStSMlp/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VDcStSMlp/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port now has installable Linux and macOS packages, hosted node and host-group\r\n  placement, hosted service workflows, SSH-managed remote lifecycle, and a first\r\n  attached-volume contract. What is still missing is a recognizable higher-level\r\n  workload outcome. K3s is now a credible next step, but only if the first slice\r\n  stays narrow: one hosted-control-plane cluster lane, fixed node roles,\r\n  stateless workloads, explicit bootstrap and access semantics, and no claims yet\r\n  about HA control planes, persistent volumes, ingress, or generic Kubernetes\r\n  distribution support.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Define one canonical hosted-first K3s cluster contract that reuses Port's existing control-plane, host-group, machine, guest, and proof vocabulary. (The epic PRD, voyage SRS/SDD, and downstream stories describe one K3s lane that builds on hosted Port primitives instead of inventing a separate orchestration model. -> Planning artifacts keep K3s attached to the canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport\u001b[0m CLI and hosted route model.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Plan and deliver the first executable stateless hosted K3s workflow. (One voyage scopes a fixed hosted topology with control-plane bootstrap, worker join, cluster access, and proof-backed verification. -> A first K3s slice is planned and ready for operator execution without requiring HA or persistence work first.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Keep the first K3s lane explicit about what it does not do yet. (Docs and planning artifacts fail fast on unsupported HA, persistence, ingress, multi-group, and SSH-first cluster claims. -> Operators can tell the boundary between the first hosted K3s lane and later Kubernetes platform work.)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Preserve the current local, hosted, SSH, machine, guest, and service surfaces while K3s is introduced. (The first K3s slice reuses canonical Port verbs and route semantics instead of introducing a second Kubernetes-only toolchain. -> Existing Port workflows remain valid and K3s feels like one more product lane, not a separate system.)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;214;247;255;48;2;0;83;104;1mSCOPE-05\u001b[0m missing voyage scope mapping for an epic in-scope item\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must define a canonical hosted K3s cluster contract that reuses the existing hosted control-plane, host-group placement, machine, and guest vocabulary rather than inventing a separate orchestration model.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must support one fixed, stateless hosted K3s workflow with control-plane bootstrap and worker-node join through canonical Port surfaces.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must expose cluster access and status through existing operator surfaces, including kubeconfig or equivalent API access and visibility into node or workload state.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must keep unsupported K3s shapes explicit, including HA, persistence, ingress, SSH-first ownership, and broader multi-group rollout.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Port must publish a proof-backed operator workflow for the first hosted K3s lane, including at least one human-reviewable artifact path.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Hosted K3s placement and lifecycle output must keep control-plane, host-group, selected-node, and rejected-node detail explicit.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - The first K3s slice must preserve current hosted machine, guest, service, local, and SSH workflows without silent behavior changes.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Verification for the first K3s slice must use repo-local techniques aligned with Keel recommendations, including Rust tests, command proofs, and one recording-backed human proof path through the proof system.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Prove shared cluster-contract, placement, and lifecycle behavior through\r\n    - Record at least one human-reviewable proof artifact through the proof system,\r\n    - Use command proofs for bootstrap, cluster access, and boundary failures.\r\n    - hosted and storage stories.\r\n    - story-level Rust tests mapped to voyage requirements.\r\n    - using the same cast or gif review pattern already established for prior\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 16 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 8 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 7 | media 1 | other 1\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVDfytSpPs\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Hosted Stateless K3s Foundations (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
